<section class="group">
   <div class="group-head">
      <h2>iPhone</h2>
   </div>
   <div class="box ios">
      <p class="note">
         With no IPA selected, the site fetches a decrypted Discord 357.0 IPA from
         dl.redeem.saarland, a third-party mirror Sunbird does not run, and checks it against a
         known SHA-256. Select your own decrypted IPA to patch that one instead. Patching happens in
         your browser with the plugins picked above.
      </p>
      <label class="file-picker">
         <input type="file" id="ipa-file" accept=".ipa,application/octet-stream">
         <span class="file-btn">Select IPA</span>
         <span class="file-label" id="ipa-label">No IPA selected, Discord 357.0 is fetched</span>
      </label>
      <button type="button" id="ipa-go">Patch IPA</button>
      <p class="warn" id="ipa-warn" hidden></p>
      <p class="err" id="ipa-err" hidden></p>
      <div id="ipa-result" hidden>
         <!-- biome-ignore lint/a11y/useValidAnchor: ipa.ts sets href to the IPA's object URL -->
         <a class="button dl" id="ipa-dl" download>Download patched IPA</a>
         <ol class="steps-list">
            <li>
               Sideload it with a tool that signs it for your device, like AltStore or Sideloadly.
            </li>
            <li>Open Discord, switch it to the new native client, then relaunch it.</li>
         </ol>
      </div>
   </div>
</section>

<style>
.ios {
   display: grid;
   gap: 12px;
   padding: 16px;
}

.note {
   font-size: 13.5px;
   color: var(--muted);
}

.warn {
   padding: 10px 12px;
   font-size: 13.5px;
   color: var(--warn);
   background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 8%, var(--surface));
   border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 35%, var(--border));
   border-radius: var(--radius);
}

.dl {
   width: 100%;
}

.steps-list {
   margin: 14px 0 0;
   padding-left: 18px;
   font-size: 13.5px;
   color: var(--muted);

   & li {
      padding: 2px 0;
   }
}
</style>

<script src="../scripts/ipa.ts"></script>
